@.str.27 = private unnamed_addr constant [2018 x i8] c"\0AA point cloud contains a list of 3D points. The point cloud class stores the\0Aattribute data in key-value maps, where the key is a string representing the\0Aattribute name and the value is a Tensor containing the attribute data.\0A\0AThe attributes of the point cloud have different levels::\0A\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A\0A    device = o3d.core.Device(\22CPU:0\22)\0A    dtype = o3d.core.float32\0A\0A    # Create an empty point cloud\0A    # Use pcd.point to access the points' attributes\0A    pcd = o3d.t.geometry.PointCloud(device)\0A\0A    # Default attribute: \22positions\22.\0A    # This attribute is created by default and is required by all point clouds.\0A    # The shape must be (N, 3). The device of \22positions\22 determines the device\0A    # of the point cloud.\0A    pcd.point.positions = o3d.core.Tensor([[0, 0, 0],\0A                                           [1, 1, 1],\0A                                           [2, 2, 2]], dtype, device)\0A\0A    # Common attributes: \22normals\22, \22colors\22.\0A    # Common attributes are used in built-in point cloud operations. The\0A    # spellings must be correct. For example, if \22normal\22 is used instead of\0A    # \22normals\22, some internal operations that expects \22normals\22 will not work.\0A    # \22normals\22 and \22colors\22 must have shape (N, 3) and must be on the same\0A    # device as the point cloud.\0A    pcd.point.normals = o3d.core.Tensor([[0, 0, 1],\0A                                         [0, 1, 0],\0A                                         [1, 0, 0]], dtype, device)\0A    pcd.point.colors = o3d.core.Tensor([[0.0, 0.0, 0.0],\0A                                        [0.1, 0.1, 0.1],\0A                                        [0.2, 0.2, 0.2]], dtype, device)\0A\0A    # User-defined attributes.\0A    # You can also attach custom attributes. The value tensor must be on the\0A    # same device as the point cloud. The are no restrictions on the shape and\0A    # dtype, e.g.,\0A    pcd.point.intensities = o3d.core.Tensor([0.3, 0.1, 0.4], dtype, device)\0A    pcd.point.labels = o3d.core.Tensor([3, 1, 4], o3d.core.int32, device)\0A\00", align 1
