@.str.122 = private unnamed_addr constant [3237 x i8] c"Function to consistently orient the normals of a point cloud based on tangent planes.\0A\0AThe algorithm is described in Hoppe et al., \22Surface Reconstruction from Unorganized Points\22, 1992.\0AAdditional information about the choice of lambda_penalty and cos_alpha_tol for complex\0Apoint clouds can be found in Piazza, Valentini, Varetti, \22Mesh Reconstruction from Point Cloud\22, 2023\0A(https://eugeniovaretti.github.io/meshreco/Piazza_Valentini_Varetti_MeshReconstructionFromPointCloud_2023.pdf).\0A\0AArgs:\0A    k (int): Number of neighbors to use for tangent plane estimation.\0A    lambda_penalty (float): A non-negative real parameter that influences the distance\0A        metric used to identify the true neighbors of a point in complex\0A        geometries. It penalizes the distance between a point and the tangent\0A        plane defined by the reference point and its normal vector, helping to\0A        mitigate misclassification issues encountered with traditional\0A        Euclidean distance metrics.\0A    cos_alpha_tol (float): Cosine threshold angle used to determine the\0A        inclusion boundary of neighbors based on the direction of the normal\0A        vector.\0A\0AExample:\0A    We use Bunny point cloud to compute its normals and orient them consistently.\0A    The initial reconstruction adheres to Hoppe's algorithm (raw), whereas the\0A    second reconstruction utilises the lambda_penalty and cos_alpha_tol parameters.\0A    Due to the high density of the Bunny point cloud available in Open3D a larger\0A    value of the parameter k is employed to test the algorithm.  Usually you do\0A    not have at disposal such a refined point clouds, thus you cannot find a\0A    proper choice of k: refer to\0A    https://eugeniovaretti.github.io/meshreco for these cases.::\0A\0A        import open3d as o3d\0A        import numpy as np\0A        # Load point cloud\0A        data = o3d.data.BunnyMesh()\0A\0A        # Case 1, Hoppe (raw):\0A        pcd = o3d.io.read_point_cloud(data.path)\0A\0A        # Compute normals and orient them consistently, using k=100 neighbours\0A        pcd.estimate_normals()\0A        pcd.orient_normals_consistent_tangent_plane(100)\0A\0A        # Create mesh from point cloud using Poisson Algorithm\0A        poisson_mesh = o3d.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_from_point_cloud_poisson(pcd, depth=8, width=0, scale=1.1, linear_fit=False)[0]\0A        poisson_mesh.paint_uniform_color(np.array([[0.5],[0.5],[0.5]]))\0A        poisson_mesh.compute_vertex_normals()\0A        o3d.visualization.draw_geometries([poisson_mesh])\0A\0A        # Case 2, reconstruction using lambda_penalty and cos_alpha_tol parameters:\0A        pcd_robust = o3d.io.read_point_cloud(data.path)\0A\0A        # Compute normals and orient them consistently, using k=100 neighbours\0A        pcd_robust.estimate_normals()\0A        pcd_robust.orient_normals_consistent_tangent_plane(100, 10, 0.5)\0A\0A        # Create mesh from point cloud using Poisson Algorithm\0A        poisson_mesh_robust = o3d.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_from_point_cloud_poisson(pcd_robust, depth=8, width=0, scale=1.1, linear_fit=False)[0]\0A        poisson_mesh_robust.paint_uniform_color(np.array([[0.5],[0.5],[0.5]]))\0A        poisson_mesh_robust.compute_vertex_normals()\0A\0A        o3d.visualization.draw_geometries([poisson_mesh_robust]) \00", align 1
