@.str.141 = private unnamed_addr constant [1557 x i8] c"Removes hidden points from a point cloud and returns a mesh of\0Athe remaining points. Based on Katz et al. 'Direct Visibility of Point Sets',\0A2007. Additional information about the choice of radius for noisy point clouds\0Acan be found in Mehra et. al. 'Visibility of Noisy Point Cloud Data', 2010.\0AThis is a wrapper for a CPU implementation and a copy of the point cloud data\0Aand resulting visible triangle mesh and indiecs will be made.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    camera_location: All points not visible from that location will be removed.\0A\0A    radius: The radius of the spherical projection.\0A\0AReturn:\0A    Tuple of visible triangle mesh and indices of visible points on the same\0A    device as the point cloud.\0A\0AExample:\0A\0A    We use armadillo mesh to compute the visible points from given camera::\0A\0A        # Convert mesh to a point cloud and estimate dimensions.\0A        armadillo_data = o3d.data.ArmadilloMesh()\0A        pcd = o3d.io.read_triangle_mesh(\0A        armadillo_data.path).sample_points_poisson_disk(5000)\0A\0A        diameter = np.linalg.norm(\0A                np.asarray(pcd.get_max_bound()) - np.asarray(pcd.get_min_bound()))\0A\0A        # Define parameters used for hidden_point_removal.\0A        camera = o3d.core.Tensor([0, 0, diameter], o3d.core.float32)\0A        radius = diameter * 100\0A\0A        # Get all points that are visible from given view point.\0A        pcd = o3d.t.geometry.PointCloud.from_legacy(pcd)\0A        _, pt_map = pcd.hidden_point_removal(camera, radius)\0A        pcd = pcd.select_by_index(pt_map)\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([pcd], point_size=5)\00", align 1
