@.str.152 = private unnamed_addr constant [1365 x i8] c"Segments a plane in the point cloud using the RANSAC algorithm.\0AThis is a wrapper for a CPU implementation and a copy of the point cloud data and\0Aresulting plane model and inlier indiecs will be made.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    distance_threshold (default 0.01): Max distance a point can be from the plane model, and still be considered an inlier.\0A\0A    ransac_n (default 3): Number of initial points to be considered inliers in each iteration.\0A    num_iterations (default 100): Maximum number of iterations.\0A\0A    probability (default 0.999): Expected probability of finding the optimal plane.\0A\0AReturn:\0A    Tuple of the plane model `ax + by + cz + d = 0` and the indices of\0A    the plane inliers on the same device as the point cloud.\0A\0AExample:\0A\0A    We use Redwood dataset to compute its plane model and inliers::\0A\0A        sample_pcd_data = o3d.data.PCDPointCloud()\0A        pcd = o3d.t.io.read_point_cloud(sample_pcd_data.path)\0A        plane_model, inliers = pcd.segment_plane(distance_threshold=0.01,\0A                                                 ransac_n=3,\0A                                                 num_iterations=1000)\0A        inlier_cloud = pcd.select_by_index(inliers)\0A        inlier_cloud = inlier_cloud.paint_uniform_color([1.0, 0, 0])\0A        outlier_cloud = pcd.select_by_index(inliers, invert=True)\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([inlier_cloud, outlier_cloud])\00", align 1
